\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- \uc2 Audi\uc2  Cuts Guidance Again, Citing Market Conditions and EV Issues\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dominic Chopping \par \uc2 488 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 November 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B9\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Audi\uc2  group cut its full-year margin guidance again as U.S. tariffs, restructuring costs and the postponement of an electric-vehicle platform weigh on profitability at the automaker.\par \par \uc2 "We are responding to the challenging overall economic situation and intensified competition with stringent cost- control measures and are continuing to work on our financial performance," \uc2 Audi\uc2  Chief Financial Officer \uc2 Jurgen Rittersberger\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The German company, part of \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2 , previously announced plans to cut as many as 7,500 jobs during the next few years in addition to plans to increase productivity, speed and flexibility at its German sites. The company plans to save more than 1 billion euros, equivalent to $1.16 billion, annually in the medium term.\par \par \uc2 Audi\uc2  group -- which comprises the \uc2 Audi\uc2 , \uc2 Bentley\uc2 , Lamborghini and Ducati brands -- said it now expects to report an operating margin of between 4% and 6%, down from 5% to 7% previously, mainly due to the current challenging market conditions and expenses related to the rescheduling of the electric platform. It had already reduced the target from between 7% and 9% during the summer.\par \par \uc2 A new platform that was going to serve as the base for new electric vehicles was being developed by \uc2 Volkswagen group\uc2  brands, including \uc2 Audi\uc2  and \uc2 Porsche\uc2 . However, development of the platform has been rescheduled after \uc2 Porsche\uc2  last month announced a strategic shift that will see it delay the launch of EVs. The platform will be technologically redesigned, leading to provisions.\par \par \uc2 It still expects revenue this year of between 65 billion euros and 70 billion euros and net cash flow at between 2.5 billion euros and 3.5 billion euros. Group vehicle deliveries to customers are expected at between 1.65 million and 1.75 million this year.\par \par \uc2 The guidance assumes there will be no supply bottlenecks for semiconductors and related components, echoing comments from its \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  parent, as the industry grapples with shortages of certain chips from a Dutch-based supplier. It also assumes U.S. import tariffs of 27.5% from Mexico and 15% from the EU for the remainder of the year.\par \par \uc2 The company reported third-quarter operating profit of 468 million euros, up from 106 million euros in the same period a year ago, with last year weighed by costs associated with closing a factory. Revenue rose 3.2% to 15.81 billion euros.\par \par \uc2 The operating margin rose to 3% from 0.7%.\par \par \uc2 Audi\uc2  is focusing on rapidly expanding its portfolio of cars, launching new EVs and strengthening its position in China with market-specific models, several of which launched over the summer. Next year, its product offensive will continue with new compact electric models, efficient full-size combustion engine-powered SUVs and high-performance RS models.\par \par \uc2 It delivered 1.18 million \uc2 Audi\uc2 -branded vehicles in the first nine months of the year, down 4.8% from a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020251101elb10001a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
