\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. Carmakers Overwhelmed\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ryan Felton And Christopher Otts By Supply Snafus \par \uc2 905 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 October 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Assembly lines inside a Michigan factory that churns out high-end Jeep SUVs ground to a halt last week and won't resume production until early next month. The cause, according to an official for the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 , is a shortage of aluminum.\par \par \uc2 Ford Motor\uc2  paused production at three plants for the same reason. Between the two automakers, thousands of workers in Michigan and Kentucky are now collecting unemployment.\par \par \uc2 The automotive supply chain -- a sprawling web of companies across the world -- is in focus in a way it hasn't been since the early 2020s, when a severe shortfall of semiconductor chips hobbled the industry. Auto executives routinely tout a lesson from that moment: Don't rely too heavily on any one supplier. Now, supplies of multiple items are gummed up at the same time.\par \par \uc2 "The confluence of issues is once in a lifetime," said \uc2 Sam Fiorani\uc2 , an analyst with consulting firm AutoForecast Solutions. "We haven't seen this happen before. The lessons learned from semiconductors should have prepared the manufacturers for some problems in the supply chain. But all these at once are unforeseen and very difficult to navigate."\par \par \uc2 All this is rattling an industry that has been hampered by billions of dollars in tariff payments and a costly pivot away from electric vehicles. Last week, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  said the EV pullback would cost it $1.6 billion. \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  unveiled a $13 billion U.S. investment plan that will help defray its tariff bill.\par \par \uc2 U.S. car sales are on pace this year to end slightly above the 15.9 million sold in 2024, according to S&P Global Mobility.\par \par \uc2 Next year doesn't look promising: Total production and sales are expected to dip, with tariffs weighing more on automakers and the average price of a vehicle remaining elevated, now around $50,000.\par \par \uc2 It wasn't all gloom and doom at the start of the year. Many in the industry felt that President Trump's tariffs wouldn't be nearly as bad as expected.\par \par \uc2 Then April came.\par \par \uc2 The White House imposed hefty tariffs -- 25% on imported vehicles and parts. Production stoppages ensued as executives hurried to crunch numbers and figure out which vehicles could be made and where.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has since eased the tariff burden, providing some relief for companies that meet standards set under a North American trade pact. It is only so much help, however. Industrywide, the cost exceeds $12 billion.\par \par \uc2 China, the main target of Trump's global trade war, hasn't made the carmaking business any easier. In retaliation for Trump's tariffs, China strangled a vital supply of rare-earth minerals. Export restrictions forced automakers to find workarounds to keep making cars. Some weighed extreme measures, such as shipping made-in-America motors to China to have magnets installed, The Wall Street Journal reported.\par \par \uc2 "The auto industry, long built on global supply chains, now finds itself at the mercy of a single nation's industrial policy," said \uc2 Michael Dunne\uc2 , a longtime China auto-industry consultant, in a newsletter last week. "This is no longer just an automaker's problem. It is a question of economic security, industrial survival, and strategic independence."\par \par \uc2 In September, a three-alarm fire hit a New York aluminum plant, knocking production offline until early next year. The stoppage has disrupted manufacturing schedules of profitable Ford models and, now, pricey Jeep sport-utility vehicles. A spokesman for \uc2 Jeep\uc2  maker \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  said it was a parts shortage that caused the shutdown of its Michigan factory but wouldn't specify the particular part.\par \par \uc2 Eric Graham, president of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  local for the idled \uc2 Jeep\uc2  plant, said it is possible the factory will be offline longer because of the aluminum shortage.\par \par \uc2 Ford will extend a pause on assembly of highly profitable three-row SUVs, the Expedition and Lincoln Navigator, at its Kentucky truck plant through Oct. 26, according to a memo obtained by The Wall Street Journal. The plant also started trimming output of F-Series Super Duty trucks, some of which can cost more than $100,000, according to factory workers.\par \par \uc2 A Ford spokeswoman declined to comment on the automaker's production moves. Ford has said it is working closely with \uc2 Novelis\uc2 , owner of the damaged aluminum plant, while exploring "all possible alternatives to minimize any potential disruptions."\par \par \uc2 At the same time, a strange and continuing geopolitical dispute is causing more concern that car production around the world could be upended in a matter of weeks.\par \par \uc2 Nexperia\uc2 , a chip maker based in the Netherlands, stopped shipments this month after the Dutch government took control of the company from its Chinese owner.\par \par \uc2 China, where 80% of \uc2 Nexperia\uc2 's products are processed before being delivered, banned the parent company from exporting out of the country. \uc2 Nexperia\uc2  said it was trying to obtain an exemption from the restrictions. European carmakers predicted they only had a few weeks of \uc2 Nexperia\uc2  chips on hand to use in production.\par \par \uc2 John Bozzella\uc2 , chief executive of the Alliance for Automotive Innovation, the top U.S. car industry group, warned that the \uc2 Nexperia\uc2  situation could deteriorate quickly and affect the global economy. "If the shipment of automotive chips doesn't resume -- quickly -- it's going to disrupt auto production in the U.S. and many other countries and have a spillover effect in other industries," Bozzella said. "It's that significant."\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020251020elak0001n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
