\par\par \b \uc2 Lilly Plans Facility to Boost U.S. Drug-Ingredient Manufacturing\b0\par\par\uc2 By Katherine Hamilton \par \uc2 347 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Eli Lilly\uc2  said it plans to build a $6.5 billion facility in Houston to make active pharmaceutical ingredients, including for a new oral weight-loss drug.\par \par \uc2 The plant will bring 615 jobs to the area, including engineers and lab technicians, as well as 4,000 construction jobs while it is being built, the company said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Eli Lilly\uc2  plans to manufacture orforglipron, its first oral, small molecule GLP-1 receptor agonist, at the facility. The company expects to submit orforglipron to global regulatory agencies as a treatment for people with obesity by the end of this year.\par \par \uc2 Orforglipron is a different active ingredient than the one found in Eli Lilly's Zepbound, its injectable GLP-1 agonist. Studies suggest orforglipron is less effective than tirzepatide, the active ingredient of the injectable version.\par \par \uc2 Eli Lilly\uc2  and its rival drugmakers have been working to develop an oral version of their weight-loss drugs in hopes that it would be popular among people who are deterred by having to inject the treatment.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  acquired \uc2 Metsera\uc2 , a company developing weight-loss pills. \uc2 Metsera\uc2  has two pill candidates expected to begin clinical trials imminently. \uc2 Novo Nordisk\uc2  has submitted an oral version of semaglutide -- the active ingredient in its injectable weight-loss drug Wegovy -- to the Food and Drug Administration for approval.\par \par \uc2 Eli Lilly\uc2 's planned site, which is expected to be operational within five years, is the second of four manufacturing sites in the U.S. that the Indianapolis pharmaceutical company plans to announce this year. Earlier this year, the company said it plans to expand its medicine production in the U.S. It is also building a site in Virginia.\par \par \uc2 Eli Lilly\uc2  has other U.S. sites in Indiana, North Carolina and Wisconsin, as well as internationally in Germany and Ireland.\par \par \uc2 Its U.S. investments come as President Trump ramps up tariffs on pharmaceuticals imported from other countries. This summer, the Trump administration placed a 15% tariff on most pharmaceuticals coming from the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250924el9o0001p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
