\par\par \b \uc2 Spirit to Furlough Cabin Workers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alison Sider \par \uc2 367 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 September 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Spirit Airlines\uc2  is planning to furlough one-third of its flight attendants, another effort by the bankrupt airline to slash expenses.\par \par \uc2 The carrier said Monday that it planned to furlough 1,800 of its roughly 5,200 flight attendants. Hundreds had already been out on voluntary leaves, but Chief Operating Officer \uc2 John Bendoraitis\uc2  said \uc2 Spirit\uc2  had reached the limit of what it could achieve through such measures.\par \par \uc2 "We need to shift our focus to a complete rightsizing of the airline, which means volume-based adjustments to our Flight Attendant group, and across our teams," he wrote in an employee message. "This is hard news, and we understand it affects not only you and your peers but also your families."\par \par \uc2 Flight attendants can volunteer for furlough, which will determine how many are involuntarily cut. Voluntary furloughs can run either six months or a year, according to the \uc2 Association of Flight Attendants-CWA\uc2 , a union that represents flight attendants at \uc2 Spirit\uc2  and other airlines.\par \par \uc2 Voluntary furloughs will take effect Nov. 1, while involuntary furloughs will take effect Dec. 1, the union said in a notice to members. "Furlough news is more than just a corporate decision; it's a deeply personal and professional upheaval," the union said.\par \par \uc2 The move means more pain for employees as \uc2 Spirit\uc2  looks to drastically scale back. It told employees last week that it planned to reduce flying capacity by 25% in its November schedule from a year earlier, leaving the airline with more planes and employees than it needs.\par \par \uc2 Spirit\uc2  last month filed for bankruptcy for a second time in less than a year. Executives said the company's first chapter 11 process failed to address all its financial issues, including costly airplane leases and high labor costs.\par \par \uc2 The carrier told pilots last week that it needed to find $100 million in annual contract savings.\par \par \uc2 Ryan Muller, chairman of the union that represents \uc2 Spirit\uc2 's pilots, told members in a note that concessions were inevitable, whether through a negotiated agreement, a judge's order, or the company's liquidation.\par \par \uc2 "That is the reality of this bankruptcy," he wrote last week. "There is no 'do nothing' option."\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250923el9n00044\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
